cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Watson's Binary-Rank Conjecture Is False: Kronecker Powers of a Rank-Five 0/1 Matrix Need Only 4^{k+o(k)} Rectangles"
abstract: >-
  Watson (2016) conjectured that the binary rank of the k-th Kronecker power
  of a particular 5 x 6 matrix M is 5^k for all k. We show
  4^k <= br(M^{(x)k}) <= 4^k (k+1)(floor(2.41k)+1) for every k. In particular
  br(M^{(x)33}) <= 4^33 * 1431 < 5^33, so the conjecture fails for every
  k >= 33, and the asymptotic rate is exactly 4, the nonnegative rank of M.
  The disproof at k = 33 and the lower bound are machine-checked in Lean 4
  with Mathlib. Research note; not peer-reviewed.
